          deckDescription: 'A 44-card deck used for Happy Families: eleven families of four cards each, for forty-four cards in total. There are no jokers; the deck is dealt out entirely. Traditionally each family has a name such as the Bakers or the Doctors.',
          suitDescription: 'The deck is organized into eleven families, each acting like a suit: for example the Bakers, the Doctors, the Greengrocers. Each family has exactly four members; players collect complete families of four to score.',
          rankDescription: 'Within each family there are four roles or ranks: typically Father, Mother, Son, and Daughter (or equivalent names). All four must be collected to complete a family; there is no relative ordering of these roles in play.',
